# Embedding Finite Metric Spaces in Hilbert Space

:toc: {
  :view: tree
  :orientation: horizontal
}
::

## Introduction
  {:label: sec-intro}

Every finite metric space embeds in Hilbert space with some distortion. This
note follows the standard random construction.

## Preliminaries
  {:label: sec-prelim}

:definition: {:label: def-distortion}
  The distortion of a map is the product of its expansion and its contraction.
::

### Random subsets
  {:label: sec-random}

We pick subsets of the points at random, as in :ref:sec-intro::.

## The embedding
  {:label: sec-embedding}

:theorem: {:label: thm-main}
  The map has distortion at most a constant times the logarithm of the number
  of points, in the sense of :ref:def-distortion::.
::

### Upper bound
  {:label: sec-upper}

Each coordinate is 1-Lipschitz, using :ref:sec-random::.

### Lower bound
  {:label: sec-lower}

This is the hard direction. It completes :ref:thm-main::.

## Discussion
  {:label: sec-discussion}

The bound in :ref:thm-main:: is tight, see :ref:sec-lower::.
